+<!-- v2: Methodology Drawer (header help icon) -->
+<div id="methodologyDrawer" class="modal" onclick="if(event.target===this)closeMethodologyDrawer()">
+  <div class="modal-box" style="max-width:680px;">
+    <div class="modal-hd">
+      <h2>Methodology &amp; Calculation Reference</h2>
+      <button class="modal-close" onclick="closeMethodologyDrawer()">&#10005;</button>
+    </div>
+    <div class="modal-body" style="padding:1rem 1.25rem;">
+      <div style="background:rgba(37,99,235,0.06);border-left:3px solid var(--accent,#3b82f6);padding:0.9rem 1rem;border-radius:8px;margin-bottom:1rem;">
+        <div style="font-size:0.74rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.06em;color:var(--muted,#94a3b8);margin-bottom:0.4rem;">Current values</div>
+        <div id="methodologyLiveValues" style="font-size:0.85rem;line-height:1.7;">Loading&#8230;</div>
+      </div>
+
+      <h3 style="font-size:0.95rem;margin:1rem 0 0.4rem;">Online status</h3>
+      <p style="font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--muted,#94a3b8);line-height:1.6;">Online = last HEARTBEAT or last PONG within the last 10 minutes. v1 also included <code>lastSeen</code> (which updates on any status) &#8212; that wrongly marked devs as online right after a successful upload even if their service crashed.</p>
+
+      <h3 style="font-size:0.95rem;margin:1rem 0 0.4rem;">Compliance week</h3>
+      <p style="font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--muted,#94a3b8);line-height:1.6;">Each week starts on Monday in the script timezone. A developer is compliant for the week when at least one SUCCESS row exists for that week. The 12-week trend chart sums compliant / failed / missing across all expected developers per week.</p>
+
+      <h3 style="font-size:0.95rem;margin:1rem 0 0.4rem;">Daily auto-generate</h3>
+      <p style="font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--muted,#94a3b8);line-height:1.6;">When a developer is first seen online on a given calendar day, a FORCE_RUN trigger is queued 10 minutes later so reports get uploaded automatically. Skipped for paused devs, devs that already have a trigger queued, and devs that already uploaded successfully today. Toggle from the Health page.</p>
+
+      <h3 style="font-size:0.95rem;margin:1rem 0 0.4rem;">Reclamation / stall threshold</h3>
+      <p style="font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--muted,#94a3b8);line-height:1.6;">A developer is "stalled" when their last heartbeat is older than 24 hours (configurable via the <code>stall_threshold_hours</code> Script Property). The hourly auto-stall scan emails the admin allowlist once per stall cycle &#8212; a new alert fires only after the dev pings again.</p>
+
+      <h3 style="font-size:0.95rem;margin:1rem 0 0.4rem;">Webhook authentication</h3>
+      <p style="font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--muted,#94a3b8);line-height:1.6;">Every uploader ping is HMAC-SHA256 signed with the shared secret. v2 tightened the replay window from 2 hours &#8594; 5 minutes, rejects future-dated timestamps (>60s ahead), and caches signatures during the validity window so a captured payload can't be replayed. Secret can be rotated via the <code>hmac_secret</code> Script Property (requires coordinated binary redeploy).</p>
+
+      <h3 style="font-size:0.95rem;margin:1rem 0 0.4rem;">v2 changelog</h3>
+      <ul style="font-size:0.82rem;color:var(--muted,#94a3b8);line-height:1.6;padding-left:1.2rem;">
+        <li><strong>v2.0</strong> &#8212; Period-aware compliance trend (12 weeks). Online-gate fix (excludes lastSeen). Logs pipeline visualizer handles non-terminal newest events. Tighter HMAC + replay cache. Soft admin allowlist via Script Properties. Per-week reminder email throttle. Daily auto-generate on first online + 10 min. Auto-stall scan. Bulk-cancel triggers. Version drift card with bulk force-update. CSV-injection guard.</li>
+        <li><strong>v1.x</strong> &#8212; Single-event terminal heuristic, lifetime online gate, 2-hour HMAC window, hardcoded admin/version constants, no auto-generate.</li>
+      </ul>
+    </div>
+  </div>
+</div>
+
